1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,923
A deployment package carries configuration and content from one Orchard Core site to another.

2
00:00:06,923 --> 00:00:10,931
In this video, you import a package from a zip file, import a

3
00:00:10,931 --> 00:00:14,820
recipe from JSON text, and see who is allowed to do either.

4
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:23,574
Every import runs a recipe on the site you are signed in to.

5
00:00:23,574 --> 00:00:27,790
A recipe is a list of steps, and each step changes something:

6
00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:32,070
the features, the settings, the content types, or the content.

7
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:35,401
A deployment package is a zip file.

8
00:00:35,401 --> 00:00:39,618
It holds the recipe, and any other files that the steps need.

9
00:00:39,618 --> 00:00:44,150
Deployment plans build packages, and a separate video covers them.

10
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:48,295
The steps run in the order of the recipe, and a step runs

11
00:00:48,295 --> 00:00:51,852
only when a feature that handles it is enabled on this site.

12
00:00:51,852 --> 00:00:55,840
When the last step has run, the site restarts with the next request.

13
00:01:00,022 --> 00:01:02,532
Let's start with Content, Content Items.

14
00:01:02,532 --> 00:01:07,442
The list shows the content of this site, and it holds no article called Spring Menu.

15
00:01:07,896 --> 00:01:11,245
Next, open Tools, Deployments, Package Import.

16
00:01:11,245 --> 00:01:17,426
The page is titled Import Deployment Package, and it has one field, labeled Select a file.

17
00:01:17,878 --> 00:01:21,731
The field accepts a zip file, or a recipe file in JSON format.

18
00:01:21,731 --> 00:01:25,754
Let's choose a package that adds one article to the site, and the

19
00:01:25,754 --> 00:01:28,248
name of the file appears in the field.

20
00:01:28,702 --> 00:01:29,837
Select Import.

21
00:01:29,837 --> 00:01:32,107
The page answers with the message:

22
00:01:32,107 --> 00:01:34,037
Deployment package imported.

23
00:01:34,037 --> 00:01:38,179
The package is extracted and its recipe runs at once, step by step,

24
00:01:38,179 --> 00:01:40,052
in the order of the recipe.

25
00:01:40,509 --> 00:01:43,921
To check the result, open Content, Content Items again.

26
00:01:43,921 --> 00:01:47,781
The article from the package, Spring Menu, is at the top of the

27
00:01:47,781 --> 00:01:50,299
list on the page titled Manage Content.

28
00:01:54,501 --> 00:01:58,750
JSON Import takes the recipe as text instead of a file.

29
00:01:58,750 --> 00:02:01,745
Open Tools, Deployments, JSON Import.

30
00:02:01,745 --> 00:02:06,761
The page has one field, an editor labeled JSON, with line numbers.

31
00:02:07,214 --> 00:02:09,420
Paste a recipe into the editor.

32
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:11,267
This recipe has one step:

33
00:02:11,267 --> 00:02:14,724
it sets the name of the site to Maple Street Bakery.

34
00:02:15,187 --> 00:02:16,427
Select Import.

35
00:02:16,427 --> 00:02:18,908
The page answers with the message:

36
00:02:18,908 --> 00:02:21,078
Recipe imported successfully!

37
00:02:21,078 --> 00:02:25,047
The recipe has run at once, and the editor is empty again.

38
00:02:25,502 --> 00:02:28,428
To check the result, open Settings, General.

39
00:02:28,428 --> 00:02:32,992
The Site name field shows the name from the recipe, Maple Street Bakery.

40
00:02:37,192 --> 00:02:40,075
Both pages run the recipe in the same way.

41
00:02:40,075 --> 00:02:43,498
A zip file can carry the files that its steps need.

42
00:02:43,498 --> 00:02:48,422
A recipe file, and the text you paste in JSON Import, carry the recipe only.

43
00:02:52,622 --> 00:02:55,470
If a step fails, the import stops at that step.

44
00:02:55,470 --> 00:02:59,662
The steps before it have already run, and the steps after it do not run.

45
00:02:59,662 --> 00:03:01,220
Package Import reports:

46
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:05,842
The import failed with the following errors, followed by what the step reported.

47
00:03:10,042 --> 00:03:14,692
Importing a recipe can change features, settings, content types, and content.

48
00:03:14,692 --> 00:03:19,398
Import Data, the permission that allows it, is marked Security Critical in the

49
00:03:19,398 --> 00:03:23,432
permissions of a role, and only administrators have it by default.

50
00:03:24,182 --> 00:03:29,916
Package Import and JSON Import appear in the menu only for users who have Import Data.

51
00:03:29,916 --> 00:03:34,716
Grant Import Data only to roles you trust, and import only packages and

52
00:03:34,716 --> 00:03:37,022
recipes from sources you trust.

53
00:03:39,022 --> 00:03:41,465
That's how you run a recipe on your site:

54
00:03:41,465 --> 00:03:45,780
from a zip package with Package Import, or from pasted text with JSON Import.

55
00:03:45,780 --> 00:03:47,132
Thanks for watching.

